  "2026-10-27T11:09:30.696Z",codex-agent,"Current review-fix source is 4930a98. Full CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40491011369 has all four npm/Bun Node 22/26 jobs queued with no assigned runners; no current-head full gate has passed or failed. Queue rules cap post-push waiting at 30 minutes, so pending checks must remain explicit rather than being reported as acceptance. A documentation-only receipt commit will preserve this status; PR 188 records its final-head run and exact pending jobs. Exact review-fix packed acceptance passed all five install modes on CLI 2026.10.26 and Bun 1.3.14: public tracker 155 items, 12 labels, one affected item/tag plus one declared filter and one mapping, 3 rows and 1078 JSON bytes; every source copy remained byte-identical. Duplication check passed across 23 authored modules with zero duplicated lines. No additional source changes or full local suites are needed while CI is queued."
  "2026-10-27T11:34:07.124Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 finding accepted. General rule: previews and read-back comparisons must call the same exported conversion as the importer write path, never a second normalization. The importer joins tag values as CSV before SDK parsing, whereas the planner used the SDK array branch and missed embedded commas. Audit covers preparation, atomic create/update/link-only writes, import validation/read-back, refresh deltas, SDK/CLI JSON/TOON and packed consumers. Provider policy names retain GitHub name semantics; opaque IDs and exact catalog bindings remain exact. Merged the one origin/main release-version commit cleanly before edits. No additional actionable non-blocking review comments were published."
  "2026-10-27T11:56:34.375Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class audit completed across the flat package source (there is no src directory). One exported importer-owned githubLabelsToTags joins the writer CSV representation and calls the SDK string tag parser. Preparation, plain and atomic create/update/link-only writes, provenance validation, refresh comparison/emission and label-plan source/stored/destination tags now share it. Provider label policy names, exact node IDs, repository locators and project field identities are different domains and keep their existing domain-specific producers/parsers. CSV SDK/CLI JSON/TOON regressions pass, including zero-tag destinations, Unicode expansion and legacy SDK array-producer data. Revert proof: independently reverting the shared converter, source expansion, stored normalization, complete destination expansion, preparation, refresh comparison, refresh delta emission, native mutation paths or provenance validation fails its regression (all nine exit 1); every production file was restored byte-for-byte. No tests were removed or weakened. Local strict health has clean history/integrity but reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew between pinned 2026.10.20 and 2026.10.27; pins remain unchanged, and complete gates are CI evidence."
  "2026-10-27T12:14:56.742Z",codex-agent,"New model file passed 2/2, including all 500 random GitHub label sets executed through prepared importer mutations and SDK read-back. It covers commas, case, spaces, normalized duplicates, Unicode, prefixes, prototype-like names, raw older-plan replay, refresh no-op/delta agreement, JSON/TOON validation, unresolved choices and stale revisions. Reverting only the planner source conversion also makes this property fail at its first mismatching source impact (exit 1), then byte-identical restoration passes the CSV regression. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and duplication pass; 24 authored modules have zero duplicated lines. Public read-only non-git snapshot f90f86f has 155 items, 12 labels, one affected stored item/tag and two declared example policies, 3 rows and 1146 JSON bytes, source unchanged. The first packed install attempt timed out before consumer assertions; retry disables optional npm audit/funding requests, with deadlines and acceptance assertions unchanged. Full release gates remain CI evidence."
  "2026-10-27T12:26:50.764Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance exposed an additional producer/validator agreement gap: host TOON omits null terminal fields, although JSON and the SDK report retain them. The shared strict output schema now declares null defaults for a completed continuation and nullable policy fields; consumers parse both JSON and decoded TOON through that one validator. Tag and mapping identities remain required, unfinished pages still require the exact continuation, and malformed expansions still refuse. The packed assertions are strengthened to compare complete validated reports for both formats, rather than counts alone. Added must-allow compact-null records and must-refuse incomplete pagination and missing/null tag identities. This changes no tag conversion or SDK state logic. Native Bun class regressions pass 2/2; the pinned-pm linked CSV regression passed, with result tracking disabled by existing project policy."
  "2026-10-27T13:03:07.872Z",codex-agent,"Completed the host-wire class through public SDK encodePmTableRows/decodePmTableRows, not a second JSON-cell decoder. Strict canonical row schemas derive the accepted table field names; metadata validates dense bounded arrays, finite integer coordinates, unique columns/coordinates and null padding, then SDK restoration is checked against the same producer schema. The 500 SDK table permutations pass for all row kinds, sparse fields and JSON-looking strings; invalid JSON, unsafe numbers and malformed metadata refuse with invalid_output. Five independent reversions (SDK restoration, terminal null, filter nulls, mapping nulls, negative-coordinate guard) each fail their regression, then restore byte-for-byte. Final focused planner/wire tests pass 12/12 with 100/100/100/100 targeted coverage of labels.ts and import-tags.ts; the earlier complete feature file passed 12/12 including the existing 500 SDK state sequences. New importer model passed 2/2 with 500 random label sets. Installation setup alone now allows 600 seconds due observed host/registry timeouts; runtime command deadlines remain 180 seconds, assertions/pins/release thresholds unchanged."
