  "2026-10-27T17:35:14.756Z",codex-agent,"The real minimum-SDK audit caught a second compatibility requirement that a decoder-only check misses: compiling every production and operational TypeScript module against published SDK 2026.10.9 fails at identity.ts because BulkItemUpdateMutation has no match field. Dropping that field would remove the existing under-lock expected-revision guard, so it is not an acceptable fix. The first decoder release is 2026.10.9, but the effective package floor must also support its existing transaction-match contract. Auditing published tarballs for the first joint release; the new packed consumer correctly failed rather than masking the incompatibility with the development SDK."
  "2026-10-27T17:40:21.977Z",codex-agent,"Published transaction tarballs establish 2026.10.17 as the first SDK with BulkItemUpdateMutation.match; releases 2026.10.9 through 2026.10.15 lack it, and 2026.10.16 was not published. Thus 2026.10.17 is the first joint contract supporting the decoder and the existing revision guard. A decoder-only floor of 2026.10.9, suggested by the review note, is insufficient for this package: the all-source typecheck demonstrated that fact without weakening or deleting the match guard. Manifest, peer and development minimum ranges are now 2026.10.17; the development SDK remains exactly locked at 2026.10.23. All 80 named SDK imports across 11 production/operational modules and the sdk, sdk/authoring and sdk/graph entry points are covered by the real-source minimum typecheck."
